<releaseinfo>0.1.0</releaseinfo>

<abstract>
<para>
&kappname; is an assistant which helps you to diagnose and fix common
problems on the &plasma; desktop: no sound, external display, network,
sleep or crashing applications.
</para>
</abstract>

<keywordset>
<keyword>KDE</keyword>
<keyword>Plasma</keyword>
<keyword>MCP</keyword>
<keyword>troubleshooting</keyword>
<keyword>assistant</keyword>
</keywordset>

</bookinfo>

<chapter id="introduction">
<title>Introduction</title>

<para>
&kappname; is made of three components:
</para>

<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><command>plasma-assist-troubleshooter</command>, a Model Context Protocol
(<acronym>MCP</acronym>) server which provides tools to diagnose and fix the desktop;</para></listitem>
<listitem><para><command>plasma-assistd</command>, a daemon which hosts the conversations with the language model;</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>a &plasma; applet which is the user interface.</para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>

<para>
Diagnostic tools are read only. Every action which changes the system needs an explicit
confirmation and can be undone.
</para>
</chapter>

<chapter id="using">
<title>Using &kappname;</title>

<sect1 id="adding-applet">
<title>Adding the Applet</title>
<para>
Add the <guilabel>Plasma Assist</guilabel> widget to a panel or to the system tray. It stays
hidden in the system tray until it is used, and it is shown while the assistant answers or
needs a confirmation. A global shortcut can be assigned in the <guilabel>Keyboard Shortcuts</guilabel>
page of the applet settings.
</para>
</sect1>

<sect1 id="scenarios">
<title>Guided Scenarios</title>
<para>
The home page lists common problems: <guilabel>No Sound</guilabel>, <guilabel>External Screen</guilabel>,
<guilabel>Internet or Wi-Fi</guilabel>, <guilabel>Computer Does Not Sleep</guilabel>,
<guilabel>Application Crashes</guilabel> and <guilabel>System Report</guilabel>. Click one of them to
start a conversation: the assistant first runs the diagnostic tools of the scenario, then explains
the cause and proposes a fix.
</para>
<para>
You can also describe your problem in the text field. Previous conversations are listed below it.
</para>
</sect1>

<sect1 id="conversation">
<title>Conversation</title>
<para>
Answers are written while they are generated. Each tool called by the assistant is shown as a card:
click it to see its arguments and its result. Use <guibutton>Stop</guibutton> to interrupt an answer,
and the back button to return to the home page (the answer continues in the background).
</para>
</sect1>

<sect1 id="quick-diagnostic">
<title>Without Language Model</title>
<para>
When no language model can be used, a scenario still runs its diagnostic tools and shows a summary
of their results, with the obvious problems they found (muted output, Wi-Fi disabled, low battery…).
Use <guibutton>Configure Language Model…</guibutton> on the home page to choose a provider and a model.
</para>
</sect1>
</chapter>

<chapter id="actions">
<title>Actions and Confirmations</title>
<para>
The assistant can change some settings: default audio device, volume, audio card profile, output of
an application, display settings (enable or disable a screen, its resolution, refresh rate, scale
or position), Wi-Fi, network connection, power profile, or restart the &plasma; shell.
Actions are disabled by default: enable <guilabel>Allow assistant to change settings</guilabel>
on the home page.
</para>
<para>
Every action is shown with a confirmation card before it is done. The description of the action is
built from its real arguments, not written by the language model. Choose <guibutton>Allow</guibutton>,
<guibutton>Deny</guibutton>, or <guibutton>Always Allow</guibutton> to not be asked again for this kind of
change (this choice is not proposed for actions which can't be undone, like restarting the &plasma; shell).
Without an answer after two minutes, the action is denied. When the applet is closed, a notification
lets you open it or deny the action.
</para>
<para>
A wrong display setting can leave a screen black or unusable: after a change of display settings,
choose <guibutton>Keep</guibutton> within 15 seconds, otherwise the previous settings are restored.
<guibutton>Revert</guibutton> restores them at once. The assistant refuses to disable the only enabled
screen.
</para>

<sect1 id="changes">
<title>History of Changes</title>
<para>
The history button of the home page lists the changes made by the assistant. Click
<guibutton>Undo</guibutton> to restore the previous state. Undo is refused when the setting was
changed again since, to not overwrite your own change.
</para>
</sect1>
</chapter>

<chapter id="privacy">
<title>Privacy</title>
<para>
Before results of tools are given to the language model, personal data are replaced by pseudonyms:
<acronym>MAC</acronym> and <acronym>IP</acronym> addresses, names of Wi-Fi and <acronym>VPN</acronym>
networks, user name, host name, and the path of your home folder. Passwords and keys of network
connections are never read.
</para>
<para>
Language models which send data to a remote server are refused by default: use a local model, for
example with <ulink url="https://ollama.com">Ollama</ulink>.
</para>
</chapter>

<chapter id="configuration">
<title>Configuration</title>
<para>
The language model is chosen in the dialog of the text generation framework, shared with other
&kde; applications. Other settings are saved in <filename>~/.config/plasma-assistrc</filename>:
</para>
<variablelist>
<varlistentry>
<term><literal>[General] AllowActions</literal></term>
<listitem><para>Allow the assistant to change settings, after a confirmation (default: false).</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><literal>[General] AllowRemoteLanguageModel</literal></term>
<listitem><para>Allow language models which send data to a remote server (default: false).</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><literal>[Privacy] FilterPersonalData</literal></term>
<listitem><para>Mask personal data in results of tools (default: true).</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><literal>[Confirmation] AlwaysAllowedTools</literal></term>
<listitem><para>Actions which are not confirmed anymore (<guibutton>Always Allow</guibutton>).</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
</variablelist>
<para>
Changes are saved in <filename>~/.local/state/plasma-assist/changes.json</filename> (50 last changes).
</para>
</chapter>

